              ⊙
              ) and rare starbursty disk (star-formation rate, SFR = 1,490 
              M
              ⊙
               yr
              −1
              ) probably undergoing secular evolution. This indicates that the maximal SFR (≳1,000 
              M
              ⊙
               yr
              −1
              ) predicted by simulations could occur during a galaxy’s secular evolution, away from major mergers.},
