              = 11.5 mag at 0′′.12 for the spectral templates of H
              2
              O and CO, significantly extending the parameter space available to moderately high spectral resolution towards small angular separation.
            
            
              Conclusions
              . Our results demonstrate the competitiveness of the new ERIS/SPIFFIER instrument for the orbital and atmospheric characterisation of exoplanets at high contrast and small angular separation.},
