	abstract = {After the Preliminary Design Review, the Calibration Unit of MORFEO, the Multiconjugate adaptive Optics Relay for ELT Observations,underwentacompletedesignoverhaul. This process was aimed at the mitigation of some critical aspects of the manufacturing,both in terms of optics and mechanics.While its optical configuration proved to be the best choice to meet the system requirements, especially on externalinterfaces, a slightly different layout has been investigated. By changing the displacement of the large beam splitters and applying small changes to a few optical elements, it would be possible to obtain a significant increase in the overall optical quality, for both the NGS and LGS arms. Moreover, some important modification to the mechanics could actually decrease the complexity of the assemblies and adjustments, also allowing a better accessibility to the system from all sides, thus facilitating the MAIT operations. We present an overview of the new layout of the MORFEO CU.},
